# Sleigh specification for the MOS 6510 (the CPU in the Commodore 64, C128, 1551 drive,
# and others), language id 6510:LE:16:default. The 6510 is a 6502 with one architectural
# addition: an on-die I/O port at $00/$01. This spec is therefore just the 6502 core plus
# the port layer; only the documented opcode set is decoded (see 6510undoc.slaspec for the
# variant that adds the undocumented NMOS opcodes).
#
# SYSTEM NEUTRALITY (bead grm-bk6): the PORT/PORTDDR registers modeled here carry NO
# banking meaning -- no LORAM/HIRAM/CHAREN, no bank-state context register. What the port
# bits do is board wiring (C64 PLA vs. 1551 drive control), so per-system interpretation
# lives in the machine descriptor and the bank analyzer, never in the language. See
# 6510port.sinc for the full rationale.

@include "6502core.sinc"
@include "6510port.sinc"
